From 8b76b06f50330c80403a0f55280f91151720f56a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:55:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] LogarithmicStrainHandler: divided differences without
 cancellation

The divided differences of the logarithm are now always computed with
log1p from the eigenvalues of C - I, also when the handler is built
from the deformation gradient. The special cases for equal eigenvalues
are removed.

The former formulas divided differences of rounded values by
differences of eigenvalues, which are of the order of the rounding
errors when two eigenvalues are close. In single precision, for a
rotated uniaxial strain of 10 % and a dual stress not coaxial with the
strain, the error was 1e-1 on the second Piola-Kirchhoff stress and
4.6e2 on its derivative. It is now below 4e-6.

The former special case of two equal eigenvalues was also inaccurate
in any precision: with two equal stretches and an anisotropic tangent
operator, the material tangent operator departed from a finite
difference by 1.4e-4 in long double (9e-8 now).

The test checks these cases, and the handlers built from the
deformation gradient in single precision.
